# ----- B-017 install funnel — same-origin Pages Functions take over -----
# - `/install.sh` is now served as a static file from `public/install.sh`
#   (Cloudflare Pages serves the file when no _redirects rule matches).
# - `/dl/<filename>` is handled by `functions/dl/[file].ts` which proxies
#   GitHub Releases through GITHUB_RELEASE_TOKEN so the install funnel
#   works while the source repo stays private.
#
# Legacy redirects below kept *intentionally non-matching* (the Function
# at `/dl/[file]` wins) — listed here as breadcrumbs for anyone who
# expected the old direct-to-GitHub flow.
#
# /dl/TARS-8.4.0-arm64.dmg → handled by functions/dl/[file].ts → GitHub via PAT
# /dl/TARS-8.4.0-setup.exe → ditto
# /dl/TARS-8.4.0.AppImage  → ditto
# /install.sh             → public/install.sh (static file, served directly)

# ----- Downloads manifest -----
# `/api/product/downloads` and `/api/product/version` are served by
# Pages Functions (`functions/api/product/{downloads,version}.ts`) so
# they live on the same origin as the SPA. Cloudflare Pages does not
# allow `_redirects` rewrites (status 200) to external origins, which
# is why the external proxy lives in code rather than here.

# ----- SPA fallback — must be last -----
# All other paths render index.html so client router takes over.
/*                 /index.html        200
